A||N||2||MR2KLR||Took apart my 4.9L today :(||||9||
Z||000000||MR2KLR||11-11-2001||05:39 PM||||<BR>I started out today To see if the intake manifold off of a 89 4.5L TBI caddy would work/ fit on the '92 SFI engine that I have I started easy and seperated the trans (TH440 I think) because I will me going with another trans and it makes it easy to move the motor around on the ground. So that pops right of no problem. Onto the Inatke manifod, I started by removeing all of the harness, distributor, Alt bracket, Power steering & PS pump, I then used shop air and blow the whole thingclean, Then removed the remaiming vac lines, coolant hoses and Fuel rail/ Injectors. instantly I could smell something bad like real bad and not a car smell, and I could see through the injector ports # 1, 3 & 5 a liquid I prayed was bad gas. I then poped off the Valve covers first the  "Rear" one then the "Front" one HORROR!!! White funky "Woil" :EEK: (My own word) water & oil all over the rockers. Ok now i'm pissed I break out the impact gun and start zinging of the rockers & girdle when I see that where the 10mm bolt on the end (front bank, trans side) is not there and that the last 1" of the thing that the rockers mount to has broken off and is not there not even floating around in the head, gone, someone broke if off and didn't say anything, just slaped it together or back together.<P>But wait it get worse. I now have all the rockers off and I made up a little pushrod holder out of a box to keep them in order. All look like they are brand new no groves or bends all perfect except Cyl # 5 & 6 intake both have the IDENTICAL groves at the botom, I think that is prety strange they have the same mark I compared them very wierd.  so now I get to pull of the intake manifold. I zing it of to cause I just don't care at this point. nothing odd water came out of the # 1 & 3 runners and I can now see that the woil level at this point and it is up to the botom of the cam  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I pop off the heads rear first and wow it's like new in there crosshached & all then the front head as soon at I touch it with the dead blow hammer water pours out on my foot I lift it off (the rusty head that is) and I can't describe how bad it looks, the only way I can even come close is "un-repair-able damage) it is looks like a Datsun Z car's fender well in there and it smels like a dead animal. that's it I stoped there. I'm now looking for another 4.9 (woil-less) all I found in my junk yard (I work there) where two 89 4.5 TBI's. but I want a 4.9 Oh well this is long :EEK:<P>Pissed off camper,<BR>      Tom||||reg||9
Z||000001||rockcrawl||11-11-2001||06:39 PM||||Hey Tom, If you can salvage the crank, rods, and pitons, you can swap them into one of those 4.5's and still have a 4.9. Also, don't toss the PFI parts when you change over to TBI or carb, there are lots of people that could use those parts.<P>Jon||||reg||1
Z||000002||MR2KLR||11-11-2001||06:52 PM||||Rockcrawl:  I thought I saw that in one of your posts but was not sure. I'll pull out the Crank & rods sometime this week. before I toss the rest I don't know about the pistons though the "Rear" 4 should be fine but if thay are made out of something that rusts the other 4 are no good, It looked like the outer hull of a ship in there. <P>I did save all of the manifold mounted PFI parts (hard vac. lines, Manifold, EGR, all manifod mounted Sensors, injectors & fuel lines/ Rails) I'd gladly cut someone a deal. Though I would love a 4.9 PFI in the '88 I'm picking up on the 26th.<P>does any body make aftermarket pistons for the caddy? can I use a set of used pistons and just Hone out a 4.5 block and slap on new rings? <P>[This message has been edited by MR2KLR (edited 11-11-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by MR2KLR (edited 11-11-2001).]||||reg||1
